<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Let Us Dream Conference provides a platform to share, learn, and celebrate people and social service groups dedicated to uplift the society. Since its inception in 2017 at Louisiana Tech University, the annual conferences have provided opportunities to engage in active conversations  grounded in community-improvement-based research, experience, and best practices. The conferences are organized by groups of volunteers and hosted in institutions across the world.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Conference is a forum for initiating a spectrum of service possibilities and intervention models to promote and support engagement in volunteerism across generations. It was established to effectively network and collaborate with volunteers, philanthropists, and community organizations, thereby empowering them in diverse community-improvement programs. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (TIt opens opportunities for students, researchers, along with practitioners to share from their knowledge and experiences. This synergizes the effort and impact towards community improvement. Volunteers from local communities participating in the conference can engage in fruitful dialogues with visionaries to strengthen their existing initiatives.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
